Gradvue MVP: Core Functions, Features & Focus
📌 Core Focus
Gradvue aims to streamline school management, focusing on:

Student administration (enrollment, class management).

Tuition tracking (payments, outstanding balances, notifications).

Teacher & subject assignments (clear role-based structure).

Parent communication (tuition alerts, academic updates).

Simple & efficient UI (for web & mobile).

🛠️ Core Functions & Features
1️⃣ User Management & Role-Based Access
Roles: Principal (or appointed proxy), Teachers, Parents, Students.

Principals/proxies can:

Manage students, classes, and subjects.

Assign teachers and define tuition structures.

Track tuition payments and outstanding balances.

Teachers can:

Manage their assigned subjects.

Input grades for students.

Parents can:

View tuition status, payments, and outstanding fees.

Receive notifications about their child’s academic performance.

Students can:

View their grades and school-related updates.

2️⃣ Student & Class Management
Add, edit, remove students and assign them to classes.

Lay out class structures (which students belong to which class).

Assign teachers to specific subjects per class.

3️⃣ Tuition & Payment Tracking
Input tuition breakdown for each student.

Track payment status (Paid, Partial, Outstanding).

Use urgency-based color coding:

✅ Green: Paid

⚠️ Yellow: Partial Payment

❌ Red: Outstanding

Send automated notifications to parents about unpaid fees.

4️⃣ Academic Tracking & Reporting
Assign teachers to subjects and classes.

Teachers input student grades.

Generate basic report cards for students.

5️⃣ Communication & Notifications
In-app notifications and alerts for payments, grades, and announcements.

Automated fee reminders for parents.

Direct messaging (optional for MVP, can be added later).

🎯 MVP Development Focus
Fast Deployment: Start with core features, expand later.

Scalability: Simple but structured database & APIs.

Security: Role-based access control using JWT authentication.

Web & Mobile Accessibility: React TypeScript for web, Flutter for mobile.
